Z||000000||merlin||08-05-2001||10:58 AM||||I recently performed a leakdown test and compression check on my 1987 V6 GT with 145,000 miles after noticing oil in my coolant and I need a little help interpreting the results to determine whether a rebuild is required or just replacement of the head gasket.<P>Cylinder  Compression(lbs)  Leakdown(%)<BR>1               150             67<BR>2               150             13<BR>3               150             30<BR>4               140             13  <BR>5               163             12<BR>6               150             11<P>Although it's obvious that the head gasket is blown between the 1 and 3 cylinder (hopefully not a cracked head), I also hear and feel air escaping from the exhaust and dipstick tube for all cylinders.  My major concern is that the piston rings are bad, given the air escaping from the dipstick tube.  However, the car has no abnormal noises and the compression seems to be great.  Another concern is how much damage has the oil in the coolant and coolant in the oil going to cause. What should I do?...  Rebuild it or just replace the head gasket?  I would like to get another 20,000 miles out of this engine before a rebuild.||||reg||5
Z||000001||starfighter007@msn.com||08-05-2001||12:17 PM||||Well I dont see the obvious that you see between #1and#3 cyl's. But yes at the very least beside the head gasket I think you should send your heads out and have them checked and while there have them perform a valve job.I dont think your rings are bad. hope thi s helps||||reg||1
